      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "H1N5",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the full adder: carry stage of half adder 1, Y = NAND(A, B), feeding H1CARRY.A. The whole full adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of A, B and Cin onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
